{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":3265953,"ns":0,"title":"Standpoint feminism","extract":"Standpoint feminism is a theory that feminist social science should be practiced from the standpoint of women or particular groups of women, as some scholars (e.g. Patricia Hill Collins and Dorothy Smith) say that they are better equipped to understand some aspects of the world.","description":"Social science theory","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}